# The external tools this repository drives, pinned.
#
# Two jobs are done by a binary rather than by a Python binding: refuting the
# leaves of a cube-and-conquer partition (Kissat — the bundled 4.0.4 wheel is
# broken on Windows, see docs/methodology.md), and building that partition
# (march_cu, which has no Python package at all).  The revisions below are what the
# measurements in RESULTS.md were produced with; `oplab.tools` finds the binaries
# and `oplab solvers` reports which implementation answered.
#
# The digest is of `git archive <revision>`, so it pins the *sources* and not the
# compiler: a gcc version or a flag changes the binary, which is why the advisory
# `binary_sha256` is separate and stays advisory.
#
# To move a pin: check the new revision out, build it with the line below, re-run
# `oplab solvers --solver kissat404` and one `scripts/cube_conquer.py` case, and
# only then edit these lines.

name kissat
source https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat
revision rel-4.0.4 (commit 8af8e56f174b778aef3aa45af9f739b2a5f492c2)
archive_sha256 4b1ba789ef75a831014e5265e69cd76d5e1ec9303a3a4ad424dc29c413b9fd79
build git clone https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat && cd kissat && git checkout rel-4.0.4 && ./configure && make -j
binary kissat/build/kissat
version_check `kissat --version` prints 4.0.4
binary_sha256 a8b7dfdf5af07d2fcc453b9ccabd1c9f5b935ebc888f1c9185914cc886505092 (advisory: x86-64 Linux, gcc 15)

name march_cu
source https://github.com/marijnheule/CnC (the march_cu/ directory)
revision CnC at 705b60c6491ef2b61988b3ce6ac674be1b90571d
archive_sha256 fbd7c5f7d599138cade24a27cd37eecdf220d3befcd048eb2f36828c4971d393 (of `git archive <rev> -- march_cu`)
build git clone https://github.com/marijnheule/CnC && cd CnC/march_cu && make CFLAGS="-std=gnu11 -O3 -fno-strict-aliasing -DNDEBUG -fcommon"
binary march-cu/march_cu
version_check has no version flag; with no argument it prints its usage line
note the CFLAGS are not optional on a current gcc: the 2012 sources use `false`,
note `not` and `first` as identifiers (keywords since C23, hence -std=gnu11) and
note rely on common symbols (-fcommon, the gcc 10+ default being -fno-common)

# On Windows, build both under WSL and point the variables at them:
#
#   OPLAB_KISSAT="wsl -e /home/me/kissat/build/kissat"
#   OPLAB_MARCH_CU="wsl -e /home/me/march-cu/march_cu"
#
# A `wsl` command is a Linux process, so `oplab.tools.wsl_path` converts the file
# paths handed to it (`D:\gen\x.cnf` becomes `/mnt/d/gen/x.cnf`, a relative path is
# resolved first); without that, a cube file written on one side is not readable
# from the other.
